WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
The Southern Song minister Wen Tianxiang was captured in the war against the Yuan and escorted to Dadu.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.078
All along the way he held his head high, his expression utterly resolute.

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:17.068
The Yuan court sent people again and again to urge him to surrender, even promising him high office and rich rewards.

00:00:17.418 --> 00:00:19.794
Wen Tianxiang did not spare them a single glance.

00:00:20.144 --> 00:00:24.752
Wen Tianxiang firmly refused, saying he would never betray the Southern Song.

00:00:25.102 --> 00:00:28.966
His answer was a single sentence: never surrender.

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.764
In prison, he wrote the timeless masterpiece, the Song of Righteousness.

00:00:34.114 --> 00:00:38.026
Under the lamplight, his brushstrokes were strong and forceful.

00:00:38.376 --> 00:00:43.848
In the end, Wen Tianxiang met his death with calm dignity, dying for the loyalty and righteousness in his heart.

00:00:44.198 --> 00:00:48.014
The morning sunlight shone into the quiet cell.

00:00:48.364 --> 00:00:52.964
His story of steadfast loyalty and righteousness has been widely told throughout Chinese history.

00:00:53.314 --> 00:00:57.442
People revere his integrity, and his story is told to this day.

